usually limited to two or probably at most three words glued together.
Finnish has no such limitations and a valid word is, for example,
lentokonesuihkuturbiiniapumekaanikkoaliupseerioppilas. (Roughly "Jet
engine assistant mechanician non-commissioned officer pupil".) Another
famous word play is "ep=E4j=E4rjestelm=E4llistytt=E4m=E4tt=F6myydell=E4ns=
=E4k=E4=E4nk=F6h=E4n"
which I once tried to translate into English. The result is here:
http://dy.fi/ij6

